---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How Renovate moves a pinned download
    accDescr: A week after a new release of gitsign, Infection, krankerl or Nextcloud, Renovate moves its version in the workflows and in .github/sign-tag.sh. Then pins.py downloads the new release and writes its sha256 beside the version and into .github/pins.toml, and Renovate commits both. The tests check that every version has the sha256 of the record. Once every check passes, the update merges on its own as fix(deps), and the next release of the blueprint brings it to every repository.

    release(["New release<br>of a tool"])
    renovate["Renovate moves the version,<br>a week after the release"]
    pins["pins.py downloads the release<br>and writes its sha256"]
    checks{"Every version has<br>its sha256"}
    merge["Merges on its own<br>as fix(deps)"]
    everywhere["The next release brings it<br>to every repository"]

    release --> renovate --> pins --> checks
    checks -- "every check passes" --> merge --> everywhere

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class release,renovate,pins,checks bot
    class merge,everywhere done
